<h1>Escape 3: Auth Doesn't Need Route Guards</h1>
<p style="color:var(--ui-text-muted);margin-bottom:2rem">Your app checks auth client-side and redirects. The escape: the server never sends the content.</p>

<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:2rem">
  <div>
    <h3 style="color:var(--ui-destructive)">At Depth (Layer 5)</h3>
    <pre style="background:#1e1e2e;color:#cdd6f4;padding:1rem;border-radius:8px;font-size:0.78rem;overflow-x:auto;line-height:1.5"><code>function ProtectedPage() {
  const { user, isLoading } = useSession();

  if (isLoading) return &lt;Spinner /&gt;;
  if (!user) {
    router.push('/login');
    return null; // flash of content before redirect
  }

  return &lt;AdminPanel user={user} /&gt;;
}

// The client bundle contains AdminPanel code
// even for unauthorized users.
// The route guard hides rendering,
// not delivery.</code></pre>
    <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--ui-text-muted);margin-top:0.5rem">The JS for the protected page ships to everyone. The guard prevents rendering, not delivery. Flash of content before redirect.</p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 style="color:var(--ui-success)">Surfaced (Layer 0)</h3>
    <pre style="background:#1e1e2e;color:#cdd6f4;padding:1rem;border-radius:8px;font-size:0.78rem;overflow-x:auto;line-height:1.5"><code>&lt;htx:auth role="admin"&gt;
  &lt;!-- Admin content here.
       This HTML only exists in the response
       if the user is an authenticated admin.
       Otherwise it was never rendered.
       View source to confirm: it's not hidden.
       It's absent. --&gt;
  &lt;h2&gt;Admin Panel&lt;/h2&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Secret admin content.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/htx:auth&gt;

&lt;htx:unauth&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Please log in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/htx:unauth&gt;</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>

<h3 style="margin-top:2rem">What dissolved</h3>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:0.5rem;font-size:0.85rem">
  <div style="padding:0.5rem;background:#fef2f2;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:line-through;color:#999">NextAuth / Auth.js</div>
  <div style="padding:0.5rem;background:#fef2f2;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:line-through;color:#999">useSession hook</div>
  <div style="padding:0.5rem;background:#fef2f2;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:line-through;color:#999">ProtectedRoute wrapper</div>
  <div style="padding:0.5rem;background:#fef2f2;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:line-through;color:#999">Client-side redirect</div>
  <div style="padding:0.5rem;background:#fef2f2;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:line-through;color:#999">Loading spinner during auth check</div>
  <div style="padding:0.5rem;background:#fef2f2;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:line-through;color:#999">Flash of protected content</div>
</div>

<h3 style="margin-top:2rem">Live: Security through absence</h3>
<htx:auth>
  <htx:component src="/ui/alert.htx" variant="success" title="Authenticated">
    You are <htx:v>auth.user.name</htx:v> (<htx:v>auth.user.role</htx:v>). This content exists in the response because the server resolved your session.
  </htx:component>
</htx:auth>
<htx:unauth>
  <htx:component src="/ui/alert.htx" variant="info" title="Not Authenticated">
    This is the guest view. The authenticated content was never rendered. View source — it is not in the HTML. Not hidden. Absent.
  </htx:component>
</htx:unauth>

<p style="margin-top:1.5rem"><a href="/layer5">&larr; Back to Layer 5 First</a></p>
